WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:17.587
Dawn broke and a fresh breeze blew through the branches of the fir trees, making the rustling sound

2
00:00:17.607 --> 00:00:18.567
that Heidi loved.

3
00:00:19.628 --> 00:00:21.870
It woke her, and she jumped out of bed.

4
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.833
Her grandfather was already outside, washing Daisy and Dusky.

5
00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:32.989
Rosy clouds were floating in the clear morning sky, and the sun was coming over the mountains.

6
00:00:33.009 --> 00:00:36.610
"What, are you awake already?"

7
00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.550
asked Grandfather when Heidi came outside.

8
00:00:40.611 --> 00:00:44.372
Heidi ran to the trees and skipped delightedly under the waving branches.

9
00:00:45.472 --> 00:00:51.174
Grandfather brought the goats out of their pen, and as soon as Heidi saw them, she ran and

10
00:00:51.214 --> 00:00:52.734
put her arms around their necks.

11
00:00:54.435 --> 00:00:56.495
Peter was whistling as he came up the path.

12
00:00:57.476 --> 00:01:01.769
His herd appeared first, and Heidi let Daisy and Dusky go join their friends.

13
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.631
Peter wanted to talk to Heidi, so he pushed his way through the goats.

14
00:01:06.651 --> 00:01:09.152
"Can you come up the mountain with me?"

15
00:01:09.532 --> 00:01:09.973
he asked.

16
00:01:09.993 --> 00:01:12.634
"I can't, Peter.

17
00:01:12.994 --> 00:01:16.555
My friends from Frankfurt might come today," said Heidi.

18
00:01:17.596 --> 00:01:18.656
Peter wasn't happy.

19
00:01:19.616 --> 00:01:23.638
Heidi had said the same thing every morning since Clara's letter arrived.

20
00:01:24.699 --> 00:01:26.919
He left with the goats without saying good-bye.

21
00:01:28.444 --> 00:01:35.369
In Frankfurt, Heidi had learned to like being tidy, so after breakfast, she cleaned the table, put the

22
00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:37.851
dishes back in the cupboard, and tidied the hut.

23
00:01:38.971 --> 00:01:43.254
Then, a sunbeam, shining through the window, seemed to call her outside.

24
00:01:44.335 --> 00:01:46.857
She ran out and lay in the fresh, warm grass.

25
00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:52.761
Grandfather followed her, but was just in time to see her running down the mountain.

26
00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:54.842
"They're here!"

27
00:01:55.263 --> 00:01:56.884
Heidi shouted over her shoulder.

28
00:01:57.952 --> 00:01:59.633
"That's the doctor in front."

29
00:02:00.654 --> 00:02:03.195
She rushed on and greeted the doctor affectionately.

30
00:02:04.816 --> 00:02:06.237
The doctor's face brightened.

31
00:02:07.238 --> 00:02:09.319
He had not expected such a happy welcome.

32
00:02:10.159 --> 00:02:15.302
He shook her hand and said, "Take me to meet your grandfather and show me where you live."

33
00:02:16.343 --> 00:02:17.584
But Heidi did not move.

34
00:02:18.724 --> 00:02:20.845
She was looking down the mountain path, puzzled.

35
00:02:20.865 --> 00:02:24.107
"Where are Clara and Grandmamma?"

36
00:02:24.528 --> 00:02:24.988
she asked.

37
00:02:26.608 --> 00:02:29.150
"I'm going to disappoint you, Heidi," he replied.

38
00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.951
"I've come alone.

39
00:02:31.992 --> 00:02:33.633
Clara has been too ill to travel.

40
00:02:34.574 --> 00:02:38.016
But they will come in the spring, as soon as the days get warmer."

41
00:02:38.937 --> 00:02:41.118
For a minute or two, Heidi couldn't speak.

42
00:02:42.079 --> 00:02:43.520
She was greatly disappointed.

43
00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:48.023
When she looked up at the doctor, there was a lonely look in his eyes.

44
00:02:49.724 --> 00:02:52.706
It made her think he was just as disappointed as she.

45
00:02:52.726 --> 00:02:57.989
"It will be spring soon," she said to cheer him up─and herself too.

46
00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:01.050
Hand in hand, they climbed to the hut.

47
00:03:02.111 --> 00:03:05.212
Grandfather put out his hand and welcomed the doctor warmly.

48
00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:10.354
The doctor seemed like an old friend because Heidi had talked about him so much.

49
00:03:12.015 --> 00:03:16.637
Grandfather had already brought the table out of the hut and had placed it in front of his

50
00:03:16.657 --> 00:03:21.458
seat. "Heidi," he said, "bring out what we need for lunch."

51
00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:26.993
To the doctor he said, "Our food is simple, but the dining room is fine!"

52
00:03:28.614 --> 00:03:34.337
As Heidi set the table, running back and forth, the doctor seemed to notice the beautiful surroundings for

53
00:03:34.357 --> 00:03:35.078
the first time.

54
00:03:35.098 --> 00:03:39.080
"Everything will taste extra good up here," he said.

55
00:03:40.641 --> 00:03:46.584
They sat down to eat, and the doctor explained all about Clara's illness and Herr Sesemann's suggestion that

56
00:03:46.624 --> 00:03:47.105
he visit.

57
00:03:48.005 --> 00:03:50.747
While they were eating, a man arrived carrying a chest.

58
00:03:51.747 --> 00:03:52.708
The doctor smiled.

59
00:03:53.484 --> 00:03:57.046
"These are presents from Clara and Grandmamma," he explained.

60
00:03:58.606 --> 00:04:04.349
Heidi was thrilled, and among all the wonderful gifts was the package of coffee that had been promised

61
00:04:04.389 --> 00:04:04.949
for Grannie.

62
00:04:05.929 --> 00:04:11.271
There was also a packet of tobacco for Grandfather, which he accepted from the doctor with a grin.

63
00:04:12.892 --> 00:04:18.414
As the afternoon ended, Grandfather walked down the mountain to help the doctor find a room in Dorfli.

64
00:04:19.375 --> 00:04:23.536
Both smoked their pipes, and Heidi went too, to deliver the coffee to
